# Copy this to `.env` and fill in what you need. Every line is optional: with
# none of them set, the credential-free Tools work exactly as they do now.
#
# `.env` is gitignored. A variable already set in your shell wins over this
# file, so a one-off `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=... pnpm mcp-auth` still overrides it.

# --- Google login (gsc_*, ga4_*, site_*, run_site_audit) ------------------
# Create an OAuth client of type "Desktop app" at
# https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials, and enable on its project
# the Search Console API, the Google Analytics Data API and the Google
# Analytics Admin API. Then run `pnpm mcp-auth` once to log in.
# See docs/setup.md for the full walkthrough.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- pagespeed_insights, crux_history and site_vitals_by_traffic ----------
# An API key from the same console, with both the PageSpeed Insights API and
# the Chrome UX Report API enabled on its project: pagespeed_insights reads its
# lab data from the first and its field data from the second, crux_history and
# site_vitals_by_traffic only the second. Neither needs a billing account.
PAGESPEED_API_KEY=

# --- web_risk_check and page_entities (billed Google Cloud APIs) -----------
# An API key from a Google Cloud project WITH BILLING ENABLED. Deliberately a
# different variable from PAGESPEED_API_KEY, so the free key never has to sit
# on a billed project. Enable on that project:
#   web_risk_check: the Web Risk API — 100,000 lookups a month free, then
#     $0.50 per 1,000 (https://cloud.google.com/web-risk/pricing).
#   page_entities: the Cloud Natural Language API — entity analysis free for
#     5,000 units a month, classification for 30,000; a unit is 1,000
#     characters (https://cloud.google.com/natural-language/pricing).
# page_entities sends the page's text to Google Cloud.
GOOGLE_CLOUD_API_KEY=

# --- domain_authority -----------------------------------------------------
# An Open PageRank API key. Sign in at
# https://openpagerank.keywordseverywhere.com/dashboard with a Keywords
# Everywhere API key (free, offered on that page) and create an OPR key there.
# The free plan covers 30,000 domain lookups a month, 60 requests a minute.
# wayback_history and brand_pageviews need no key at all.
OPEN_PAGERANK_API_KEY=

# --- Optional enrichment: seo_geo_score and ai_visibility_score ----------
# A Knowledge Graph Search API key. Without it the entity check in those two
# Tools reports as not evaluated rather than refusing; every other Tool is
# unaffected. Free.
GOOGLE_KG_API_KEY=

# --- Storage --------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the SQLite database lives. Defaults to db/thatseoagent.sqlite.
# Set to `off` to run with no persistence at all.
# TSA_DB_PATH=
